.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt HARNESSATOR.LOCK 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm harnessator.lock
.Nd committed resolution record for harnessator-managed projects
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The lockfile is generated by
.Dq harnessator setup / update
and hand-edited never.
It pins what the project config requested: exact commits for every source
and one content digest per enabled component, making agent-config drift an
ordinary, reviewable code change.
While any source is in dev mode the lock is deliberately
.Em not
rewritten - local development state must never become a committed pin.
.Pp
The file starts with a
.Dq generated ... do not edit
header comment;
.Nm Cm verify
recomputes digests from the store and fails on any difference.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic schema Ar int
format version, currently 1.
.It Xo Ic [[source]] :
.Ic name ,
.Ic git ,
.Ic range
(the config ref),
.Ic resolved
(the tag, or the branch name),
.Ic sha
(40-hex commit actually exported)
.Xc
one per declared source, sorted by name.
Branch refs record the branch head at resolve time; tag ranges the newest
matching tag.
.It Xo Ic [[component]] :
.Ic id
.Dq Ar source:category/name ,
.Ic source ,
.Ic sha
(the source commit it came from),
.Ic digest
.Dq sha256: Ns Ar hex
.Xc
one per enabled component, sorted by id.
Directory components hash order-independently over their relative paths
and file digests; single files are hashed directly; symlinks inside trees
hash their stored target text.
.El
.Sh INTEGRITY
The store checkout carries a
.Pa .harnessator-checkout
marker holding the commit; verify checks markers and digests together.
A digest difference means either a ref moved (legitimate:
.Nm Cm update )
or content changed under the same commit (never legitimate for pinned
data - investigate who edited the store).
.Sh EXAMPLE
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# harnessator.lock - generated by "harnessator update"; do not edit.
schema = 1

[[source]]
  name     = "corp"
  git      = "https://git.example.com/ai/corp-tools.git"
  range    = "~v1.2"
  resolved = "v1.2.3"
  sha      = "4f9a1b2c3d4e5f60718293a4b5c6d7e8f90a1b2c"

[[component]]
  id     = "corp:rule/security-baseline"
  source = "corp"
  sha    = "4f9a1b2c3d4e5f60718293a4b5c6d7e8f90a1b2c"
  digest = "sha256:9e2f6a1b0c4d7e5a3f8b1c2d4e6f7a8b9c0d1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b1c2d3e4"
.Ed
.Sh "SEE ALSO"
.Xr harnessator 1 ,
.Xr harnessator.toml 5
